{"id":"258ba57a-664e-45c8-aba0-67573c6b5fbe","object":"chat.completion","created":1784885343,"model":"deepseek-v4-flash","choices":[{"index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","content":"{\n  \"implementation\": \"def solve(case):\\n    nodes = case['nodes']\\n    core = case['core_distance']\\n    distances = case['distances']\\n    \\n    # Validate nodes and core distances\\n    if not all(n in core for n in nodes):\\n        raise ValueError('Missing core distance for some node')\\n    \\n    # Build mutual reachability edges, canonicalize undirected endpoints\\n    edges = []\\n    seen = set()\\n    for u, v, d in distances:\\n        if u > v:\\n            u, v = v, u\\n        if (u, v) in seen:\\n            continue\\n        seen.add((u, v))\\n        mut = max(core[u], core[v], d)\\n        edges.append((mut, u, v))\\n    \\n    # Sort by weight then endpoint IDs\\n    edges.sort(key=lambda x: (x[0], x[1], x[2]))\\n    \\n    # Union-Find\\n    parent = {n: n for n in nodes}\\n    rank = {n: 0 for n in nodes}\\n    \\n    def find(x):\\n        while parent[x] != x:\\n            parent[x] = parent[parent[x]]\\n            x = parent[x]\\n        return x\\n    \\n    def union(x, y):\\n        rx, ry = find(x), find(y)\\n        if rx == ry:\\n            return False\\n        if rank[rx] < rank[ry]:\\n            parent[rx] = ry\\n        elif rank[rx] > rank[ry]:\\n            parent[ry] = rx\\n        else:\\n            parent[ry] = rx\\n            rank[rx] += 1\\n        return True\\n    \\n    mst_edges = []\\n    total_weight = 0.0\\n    \\n    for weight, u, v in edges:\\n        if union(u, v):\\n            mst_edges.append([u, v, weight])\\n            total_weight += weight\\n            if len(mst_edges) == len(nodes) - 1:\\n                break\\n    \\n    if len(mst_edges) != len(nodes) - 1:\\n        raise ValueError('Graph is disconnected or missing edges')\\n    \\n    return {\\n        'mst_edges': mst_edges,\\n        'total_weight': total_weight\\n    }\"\n}","reasoning_content":"We need to implement solve(case) that computes MST using mutual reachability distance. The payload contains nodes list, core_distance dict, distances list (list of [node1, node2, distance]) and _case_nonce (unused). So we need to compute mutual reachability for each unique pair: max(core[node1], core[node2], distance). Then run Kruskal's algorithm on all edges (undirected, each pair once). We need to sort edges by weight, then by endpoint IDs (as strings) to break ties deterministically. Use union-find with path compression and union by rank. Collect edges until we have |nodes|-1 edges. If graph is disconnected (i.e., cannot get enough edges), raise ValueError. Return {\"mst_edges\": list of [node1, node2, weight] (weight number), \"total_weight\": sum of weights}. Ensure edge endpoints are sorted alphabetically for canonical representation? The spec: \"Canonicalize undirected endpoints.\" Probably means for each edge we should store the two nodes in sorted order (as strings) to have deterministic representation. Also sorting edges: \"Sort by reachability then endpoint IDs.\" So first sort by weight, then by first node, then second node (or both). Use tuple (weight, node1, node2). Also \"All ranking and traversal ties use the source position or identifier specified above; never depend on hash-map iteration.\" So we must sort keys. Also distances list might not include all pairs? But the problem says we have registered distance matrices, so presumably all pairs? But we must compute for all pairs from distances list, but distances list may not be exhaustive? However in public fixtures, it's complete for 5 nodes (10 edges). So we assume distances list covers all unordered pairs. If not, we would need to consider missing pairs? But spec says \"Compute core distances, mutual-reachability edge weights, and a deterministic minimum spanning tree for registered distance matrices.\" So we assume distances list is complete.\n\nEdge cases: duplicate entries? Not likely. We'll create graph with all edges from distances list. Also core_distance must exist for all nodes. If not, raise ValueError.\n\nImplementation in Python: define solve(case) that extracts nodes, core, dists. Validate all nodes present in core. Build list of edges: for each (u,v,d) in dists, compute mutual = max(core[u], core[v], d). Then create edge tuple (node1, node2, mutual) with node1 <= node2 (canonicalize). Then add to list. Then sort edges by (mutual, node1, node2). Then Union-Find: parent dict, rank dict. Initialize each node as own parent. For edge in sorted edges, find roots; if different, union and add to mst list and add weight to total. Stop when len(mst_edges) == len(nodes)-1. If after processing all edges we don't have enough, raise ValueError.\n\nReturn result in required JSON.\n\nNow output JSON: {\"implementation\": \"def solve(case):\\n    ...\"}. Need to escape properly.\n\nWe'll write the code with proper indentation.\n\nAlso note: \"Do not mutate case\". So we'll not modify input.\n\nWe'll write solve function that returns dict.\n\nWe'll include validation: check that nodes list and core dict have matching keys; that distances list items are lists of length 3; that all edge endpoints are in nodes; etc. But minimal validation is okay.\n\nWe'll raise ValueError for invalid inputs. The spec: \"Raise ValueError for an infeasible or structurally invalid case instead of silently repairing it.\"\n\nWe'll implement deterministic tie-breaking.\n\nNow produce final JSON."},"logprobs":null,"finish_reason":"stop"}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":2021,"completion_tokens":1322,"total_tokens":3343,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":512},"completion_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":770},"prompt_cache_hit_tokens":512,"prompt_cache_miss_tokens":1509},"system_fingerprint":"fp_8b330d02d0_prod0820_fp8_kvcache_20260402"}